# Source is text, and git should treat it as text even when it briefly is not.
#
# Three element files spent a week as `Bin` in every diff because a generation
# script wrote a literal NUL where a unicode escape was meant. Nobody could have
# reviewed them, and nobody noticed — which in a repository this careful about
# reviewable artifacts is the whole lesson. `make check` now refuses a NUL in
# tracked source; this is the second line of defence.
*.rs   text diff
*.js   text diff
*.toml text diff
*.json text diff
*.md   text diff
*.html text diff
